##) Tags:
---------

*) Tags are used to run the required tasks from a playbook instead of running all the tasks.
*) You can give whatever tag name you want, ra. No need to configure or declare it outside the playbook before hand.❤️

Example:

- name: Install nginx
  ansible.builtin.package:
    name: nginx
    state: present
  tags:
    - deployment

- name: service start
  ansible.builtin.service:
    name: nginx
    state: started
 
- name: Copy nginx configuration
  ansible.builtin.copy:
    src: nginx.conf
    dest: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf

- name: Create application directory
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: /opt/myapp
    state: directory
  tags:
    - deployment
	
	
ansible-playbook main.yml --tags deployment -->  So the tasks only that are with the tag 'deployment' will be executed

*)Usually, If we run the playbook normally without tags then all the tasks in the playbook will execute in the order they are written.

ansible-playbook main.yml



#) --tags:
----------

*) We use '--tags' while running the playbook to run tasks that are with a particular tag.

Example:

ansible-playbook main.yml --tags deployment

#) --skip-tags:
----------------

*)It skip the tasks that are with the 'tags' and run the other tasks in playbook. 

Example:

ansible-playbook main.yml --skip-tags config

So, the tasks that are with the tag 'config' will be skipped 


##) Tags can be applied at different levels:
--------------------------------------------

1) Task level:

- name: Install nginx
  ansible.builtin.package:
    name: nginx
    state: present
  tags:
    - deployment


2) Block level:

- block:

    - name: Install nginx
      ansible.builtin.package:
        name: nginx
        state: present

    - name: Start nginx
      ansible.builtin.service:
        name: nginx
        state: started

  tags:
    - nginx


3) Play level:

- hosts: frontend
  tags:
    - web-setup

  tasks:

    - name: Install nginx
      ansible.builtin.package:
        name: nginx
        state: present


4) Role level:

- hosts: frontend
  roles:
    - role: nginx
      tags:
        - nginx


*) We can run and skip the tags that are applied at task, block, play and role levels whenever we want based on our need.


