ANSIBLE VAULT COMMANDS:
-----------------------

1) CREATE:

ansible-vault create fileName

What happens:

1. Creates a new encrypted vault file with the given filename
2. Ansible asks you to enter a Vault password.
3. It opens the file in an editor.
4. You add sensitive data, such as passwords.
5. When you save and exit, Ansible encrypts the file and stores it


2) ENCRYPT:

ansible-vault encrypt fileName

--> Encrypts an existing plain-text file.
--> Need to set the Vault password.
--> The file will be converted into encrypted format.


3) DECRYPT:

ansible-vault decrypt fileName

--> Decrypts an encrypted Vault file.
--> Need to provide the Vault password.
--> The file will be converted back to readable format.


4) VIEW:

ansible-vault view fileName

--> Displays the encrypted file data but you need to provide the Vault password to view the data.
--> The file remains encrypted.


5) REKEY:

ansible-vault rekey fileName

--> Changes the Vault password of an encrypted file.
--> Need to provide the current Vault password and Then set the new Vault password.


6) EDIT:

ansible-vault edit fileName

--> Opens the encrypted file for editing.
--> Need to provide the Vault password to edit the data.
--> After saving, the file remains encrypted.


7) DELETE:

rm fileName

--> Deletes the Vault file.
--> Vault password is NOT required.

